Cluster_PKM_1	NeST	Cluster_PKM_1	BNIP3 DDIT4 EGLN EGLN1 EGLN3 HIF1A MIR210HG VEGFA	8	Hypoxia Sensing and Adaptive Response	This system prominently features components regulated by or regulating **hypoxia-inducible factors (HIFs)**. *HIF1A*, *EGLN1*, *EGLN3*, *MIR210HG*, *VEGFA*, *BNIP3*, and *DDIT4* are core mediators of the transcriptional and metabolic response to low oxygen conditions. *EGLNs* hydroxylate HIF1A under normoxia, while *HIF1A* activates genes that enhance glycolytic flux, angiogenesis (*VEGFA*), and survival during hypoxic stress (*BNIP3*, *MIR210HG*). *DDIT4* connects hypoxia to mTOR inhibition, reducing energy expenditure. These factors establish a functional axis adapting metabolism and signaling to oxygen availability. 	0.79	"This system prominently features components regulated by or regulating **hypoxia-inducible factors (HIFs)**. *HIF1A*, *EGLN1*, *EGLN3*, *MIR210HG*, *VEGFA*, *BNIP3*, and *DDIT4* are core mediators of the transcriptional and metabolic response to low oxygen conditions. *EGLNs* hydroxylate HIF1A under normoxia, while *HIF1A* activates genes that enhance glycolytic flux, angiogenesis (*VEGFA*), and survival during hypoxic stress (*BNIP3*, *MIR210HG*). *DDIT4* connects hypoxia to mTOR inhibition, reducing energy expenditure. These factors establish a functional axis adapting metabolism and signaling to oxygen availability. [1][2][3]

