Cluster_AKAP8_1	NeST	Cluster_AKAP8_1	CRY2 NR1D1 PER2 PER3	4	Circadian Control of Metabolic Regulation	This system includes multiple components of the circadian clock (*PER2, PER3, CRY2, NR1D1*), which regulate daily oscillations of gene expression in metabolic tissues. These transcriptional regulators control the rhythmic expression of key metabolic enzymes and transporters, thereby orchestrating the timing of energy storage, mobilization, and hormonal signaling across the light-dark cycle. Their co-presence with nutrient transporters and signaling proteins suggests functional integration in time-dependent metabolic homeostasis. 	0.74	"This system includes multiple components of the circadian clock (*PER2, PER3, CRY2, NR1D1*), which regulate daily oscillations of gene expression in metabolic tissues. These transcriptional regulators control the rhythmic expression of key metabolic enzymes and transporters, thereby orchestrating the timing of energy storage, mobilization, and hormonal signaling across the light-dark cycle. Their co-presence with nutrient transporters and signaling proteins suggests functional integration in time-dependent metabolic homeostasis. [1][2][3]

