Cluster_AKAP8_2	NeST	Cluster_AKAP8_2	ADCY5 INSR SLC2A4	3	Insulin Signaling and Glucose Transport	Key metabolic effectors such as *INSR* (insulin receptor), *SLC2A4* (GLUT4), and *ADCY5* (adenylate cyclase 5) are central to insulin-stimulated glucose uptake in skeletal muscle and adipose tissue. *SLC2A4* translocates to the membrane in response to insulin signaling via *INSR*, facilitating glucose entry into cells. *ADCY5* contributes to cAMP-mediated modulation of insulin secretion and signaling. These proteins form a coordinated module that transduces insulin signals to regulate glucose utilization, strongly linking this system to energy metabolism. 	0.74	"Key metabolic effectors such as *INSR* (insulin receptor), *SLC2A4* (GLUT4), and *ADCY5* (adenylate cyclase 5) are central to insulin-stimulated glucose uptake in skeletal muscle and adipose tissue. *SLC2A4* translocates to the membrane in response to insulin signaling via *INSR*, facilitating glucose entry into cells. *ADCY5* contributes to cAMP-mediated modulation of insulin secretion and signaling. These proteins form a coordinated module that transduces insulin signals to regulate glucose utilization, strongly linking this system to energy metabolism. [1]

