Cluster_AKAP8_3	NeST	Cluster_AKAP8_3	COQ10A DAGLA DGKD FAAH SREBF1	5	Fatty Acid and Lipid Homeostasis	Genes like *FAAH* (fatty acid amide hydrolase), *DAGLA* (diacylglycerol lipase alpha), *DGKD* (diacylglycerol kinase delta), *SREBF1* (a transcriptional regulator of lipid biosynthesis), and *COQ10A* (coenzyme Q10 biosynthesis) contribute to lipid signaling and storage. Their integration suggests the system supports lipid flux coordination, particularly in metabolically active tissues where insulin and circadian signals converge. 	0.74	"Genes like *FAAH* (fatty acid amide hydrolase), *DAGLA* (diacylglycerol lipase alpha), *DGKD* (diacylglycerol kinase delta), *SREBF1* (a transcriptional regulator of lipid biosynthesis), and *COQ10A* (coenzyme Q10 biosynthesis) contribute to lipid signaling and storage. Their integration suggests the system supports lipid flux coordination, particularly in metabolically active tissues where insulin and circadian signals converge. [1]

