Cluster_AKAP8_4	NeST	Cluster_AKAP8_4	CKMT2 L2HGDH SLC22A5 SLC45A3 SLC46A1	5	Metabolite Transport and Mitochondrial Function	Solute carrier proteins (*SLC22A5, SLC45A3, SLC46A1*) and enzymes like *L2HGDH* and *CKMT2* indicate participation in mitochondrial metabolism and organic solute transport. These molecules sustain energy production by managing the import and export of critical cofactors, such as carnitine (*SLC22A5*), which is essential for fatty acid β-oxidation. *CKMT2* couples ATP production to energy-demanding processes in tissues like heart and muscle. 	0.74	"Solute carrier proteins (*SLC22A5, SLC45A3, SLC46A1*) and enzymes like *L2HGDH* and *CKMT2* indicate participation in mitochondrial metabolism and organic solute transport. These molecules sustain energy production by managing the import and export of critical cofactors, such as carnitine (*SLC22A5*), which is essential for fatty acid β-oxidation. *CKMT2* couples ATP production to energy-demanding processes in tissues like heart and muscle. [1]

