Cluster_PAX5_1	NeST	Cluster_PAX5_1	CD79A CD80 IGHM IGHV IGKV IGLJ IGLV LAT LAT2 LCK MS4A1 PDCD1 TRAV19 TRBV20OR9	14	Lymphocyte Activation and Differentiation	Multiple immunoglobulin variable genes (e.g., *IGHV*, *IGLV*, *IGKV*, *IGLJ*, *IGHM*) are represented, indicating a system centered on **B-cell receptor diversification and clonal selection**. Accompanying these are genes like *CD79A* and *MS4A1* (CD20), which are critical for B-cell receptor (BCR) signaling and maturation. *T-cell signaling* is also prominently featured, as indicated by *CD80*, *LAT*, *LAT2*, *LCK*, *TRAV19*, *TRBV20OR9-2*, and *PDCD1*. These genes mediate TCR signal transduction, co-stimulation, and T-cell exhaustion or tolerance. The co-presence of both B-cell and T-cell lineage-specific components suggests this system supports **bidirectional crosstalk and co-regulation between adaptive immune arms**. 	0.78	"Multiple immunoglobulin variable genes (e.g., *IGHV*, *IGLV*, *IGKV*, *IGLJ*, *IGHM*) are represented, indicating a system centered on **B-cell receptor diversification and clonal selection**. Accompanying these are genes like *CD79A* and *MS4A1* (CD20), which are critical for B-cell receptor (BCR) signaling and maturation. *T-cell signaling* is also prominently featured, as indicated by *CD80*, *LAT*, *LAT2*, *LCK*, *TRAV19*, *TRBV20OR9-2*, and *PDCD1*. These genes mediate TCR signal transduction, co-stimulation, and T-cell exhaustion or tolerance. The co-presence of both B-cell and T-cell lineage-specific components suggests this system supports **bidirectional crosstalk and co-regulation between adaptive immune arms**. [1][2]

