Cluster_PAX5_3	NeST	Cluster_PAX5_3	CARD11 DYRK1B GNLY NKG7 PIK3R5 RASGRP2 TRIM61	7	Signal Transduction and Effector Function	Downstream signaling components such as *CARD11*, *PIK3R5*, *RASGRP2*, *DYRK1B*, and *TRIM61* integrate antigen receptor stimulation into transcriptional programs. These effectors interface with the NF-κB and MAPK pathways, promoting immune cell activation, proliferation, and survival. Effector molecules such as *GNLY* (granulysin) and *NKG7* highlight the cytotoxic arm of lymphocyte function, suggesting that this network extends into **cell-mediated cytotoxicity**. 	0.78	"Downstream signaling components such as *CARD11*, *PIK3R5*, *RASGRP2*, *DYRK1B*, and *TRIM61* integrate antigen receptor stimulation into transcriptional programs. These effectors interface with the NF-κB and MAPK pathways, promoting immune cell activation, proliferation, and survival. Effector molecules such as *GNLY* (granulysin) and *NKG7* highlight the cytotoxic arm of lymphocyte function, suggesting that this network extends into **cell-mediated cytotoxicity**. 

