Cluster_PAX5_4	NeST	Cluster_PAX5_4	H19 IFNG JARID2 MIR142 MIR17HG MIR3916 RAD51 SNORA1 SNORA73	9	Non-coding RNAs and Regulatory Elements	Several long non-coding RNAs (e.g., *MIR17HG*, *IFNG-AS1*, *H19*, *RAD51-AS1*, *JARID2-AS1*) and small RNAs (*MIR142*, *MIR3916*, *SNORA1*, *SNORA73*) are known to regulate transcriptional activity, splicing, and translation in immune contexts. For example, *MIR17HG* and *IFNG-AS1* are involved in **T-cell polarization and cytokine regulation**. Y\_RNAs and RN7SK pseudogenes suggest modulation of RNA stability and chromatin remodeling, potentially linking transcriptional burst control to immune activation. 	0.78	"Several long non-coding RNAs (e.g., *MIR17HG*, *IFNG-AS1*, *H19*, *RAD51-AS1*, *JARID2-AS1*) and small RNAs (*MIR142*, *MIR3916*, *SNORA1*, *SNORA73*) are known to regulate transcriptional activity, splicing, and translation in immune contexts. For example, *MIR17HG* and *IFNG-AS1* are involved in **T-cell polarization and cytokine regulation**. Y\_RNAs and RN7SK pseudogenes suggest modulation of RNA stability and chromatin remodeling, potentially linking transcriptional burst control to immune activation. [1]

